WEBVTT

00:00.333 --> 00:06.169
Episode 10
Inuki

00:07.908 --> 00:10.172
Dear Grandma,
how are you doing?

00:11.311 --> 00:13.302
I've been in Tokyo
for half a month.

00:13.413 --> 00:15.973
Both Inuki and I
are doing well.

00:16.082 --> 00:19.813
I met Princess Hinoto and Mr. Saiki
under the Diet building,

00:19.920 --> 00:23.219
as well as Arashi
and Sorata of the Seven Seals.

00:23.323 --> 00:25.416
I have also met Kamui.

00:26.860 --> 00:27.849
I was surprised...

00:27.961 --> 00:31.829
...that Kamui was so different
from the image I had of him.

00:31.932 --> 00:35.993
He's still in high school,
and I thought he was very cute.

00:36.102 --> 00:38.662
A Dragon of Earth made
a mess when I got there,

00:38.772 --> 00:41.332
but the days have
been quiet since then.

00:42.442 --> 00:44.740
What pleased me
most about Tokyo...

00:44.844 --> 00:48.837
...above all, was when I found
someone who could see Inuki.

00:49.950 --> 00:52.384
I was so happy that I cried.

00:53.486 --> 00:57.547
The Dragons of Heaven
could also see him,

00:57.657 --> 01:00.182
but it was very
special when I met him.

01:06.166 --> 01:08.259
A strange dog, but a good dog.

01:12.138 --> 01:13.196
Hey...

01:13.306 --> 01:15.570
is something wrong,
little lady?

01:15.675 --> 01:17.404
Did I do something bad?

01:22.449 --> 01:23.507
That man...

01:25.185 --> 01:28.643
I should've at least asked
for his name, right, Inuki?

01:30.490 --> 01:31.479
Hello?

01:31.591 --> 01:33.286
Is this Yuzuriha?

01:33.393 --> 01:35.293
It's me, Saiki.

01:35.395 --> 01:37.454
Oh, hello, what's going on?

01:37.564 --> 01:40.397
Well, are you free today?

01:42.135 --> 01:45.593
If you don't mind,
I'd like you to come with me.

01:47.140 --> 01:48.903
Is that, by any chance...

01:49.009 --> 01:51.239
Are you asking
me out on a date?

01:52.946 --> 01:54.811
Seiichiro Aoki...

01:54.914 --> 01:57.508
This is the business card
Arashi received.

01:57.617 --> 02:02.816
Apparently, he claimed to be
one of the Seven Seals like you.

02:02.922 --> 02:05.117
Oh, I see.

02:05.225 --> 02:08.092
Considering the event
beneath the Diet building...

02:08.194 --> 02:11.823
...we must gather all the Seals
as soon as possible.

02:12.932 --> 02:17.699
Arashi and Sorata headed over
to Kamakura to see one of them.

02:17.804 --> 02:21.797
So in the meantime, we need
to see this person as well.

02:22.909 --> 02:25.104
I hope he's
a wonderful person.

02:25.211 --> 02:27.771
Well, I don't think
he's that great.

02:29.182 --> 02:31.173
Oh, well, actually...

02:31.284 --> 02:33.411
I know him.

02:33.520 --> 02:35.886
I haven't seen him
in many years...

02:35.989 --> 02:38.184
But he's my uncle.

02:38.291 --> 02:39.690
Is that so?

02:39.793 --> 02:42.455
Then he's definitely wonderful!

02:42.562 --> 02:45.725
Because if he's your relative,
he has to be!

02:47.434 --> 02:48.731
T-That's not true.

03:00.113 --> 03:02.980
It looks like it will
take a while yet.

03:03.083 --> 03:07.042
He can't come until some
author's manuscripts are done.

03:07.153 --> 03:10.520
Editorial work is
really tough, isn't it?

03:10.623 --> 03:11.647
What should we do?

03:11.758 --> 03:13.589
Shall we postpone
till tomorrow?

03:13.693 --> 03:15.558
No, I'm all right.

03:15.662 --> 03:17.459
I can wait
no matter how long.

03:17.564 --> 03:19.589
I want to meet him soon.

03:19.699 --> 03:21.291
I'm sorry...

03:21.401 --> 03:23.892
Mr. Saiki,
would you like ice cream?

03:25.438 --> 03:27.497
That sounds good.

03:27.607 --> 03:29.871
I know a yummy place
around here.

03:29.976 --> 03:33.070
I'll go buy some,
so please stay here!

03:33.179 --> 03:34.077
I'll...

03:53.199 --> 03:54.097
Inuki?

03:55.235 --> 03:56.759
What's wrong, Inuki?

04:02.876 --> 04:03.774
You're kidding...

04:12.419 --> 04:14.353
H-Hello.

04:14.454 --> 04:16.046
Y-Yo.

04:16.156 --> 04:18.818
I'm sorry about the other day.

04:18.925 --> 04:21.723
My sudden crying
surprised you, right?

04:21.828 --> 04:23.386
Y-Yeah.

04:23.496 --> 04:25.157
I was slightly surprised.

04:25.265 --> 04:26.698
I'm sorry.

04:26.800 --> 04:29.030
But it was the first time...

04:29.135 --> 04:34.198
I was so happy that I met
someone who could see my Inuki...

04:34.307 --> 04:37.242
Well, other people
can't see Inuki, right?

04:37.343 --> 04:38.571
I see.

04:38.678 --> 04:40.168
So that's what it was.

04:40.280 --> 04:43.010
I'm Yuzuriha Nekoi.

04:43.116 --> 04:45.983
Can you tell me your name?

04:46.085 --> 04:47.712
S-Sure.

04:47.821 --> 04:49.914
I'm Kusanagi Shiyu.

04:50.023 --> 04:51.752
Kusanagi Shiyu.

04:51.858 --> 04:53.223
That's right.

04:53.326 --> 04:55.988
Do you live around here?

04:56.095 --> 04:59.064
In the base at Ichigaya.

04:59.165 --> 05:00.962
I'm with the Self-Defense Force.

05:01.067 --> 05:02.125
The SDF!

05:02.235 --> 05:06.365
Wow, I've never talked to
a member of the SDF before!

05:10.210 --> 05:14.078
And I've never talked to
a schoolgirl all alone, either.

05:17.750 --> 05:19.274
Today's your day off?

05:19.385 --> 05:20.443
Yeah.

05:20.553 --> 05:23.647
I always walk around
this area on my days off.

05:24.924 --> 05:26.721
He really is a good dog.

05:29.996 --> 05:34.558
I grew up together with Inuki at
Mitsumine Shrine since I was little.

05:34.667 --> 05:40.401
But I couldn't understand that
he was invisible to everyone then.

05:40.507 --> 05:42.566
Well, he is a special dog.

05:43.676 --> 05:46.770
I'm meeting up
with someone now,

05:46.880 --> 05:49.405
but I still have
time before he comes.

05:49.516 --> 05:53.282
Would you listen to
the story about me and Inuki?

05:53.386 --> 05:55.513
I don't mind...

05:55.622 --> 05:58.614
I would like you
to hear it, Mr. Shiyu.

05:58.725 --> 06:00.659
Just call me Kusanagi.

06:00.760 --> 06:03.524
In either case, it's a
strange name anyway.

06:05.164 --> 06:07.029
When I was a child...

06:08.301 --> 06:10.292
...everyone called me a liar.

06:11.905 --> 06:13.805
Nobody could see Inuki...

06:15.008 --> 06:17.533
Nobody would understand...

06:17.644 --> 06:21.410
They all said I talked
about a dog that didn't exist.

06:21.514 --> 06:25.780
And when I was in third grade,
something happened.

06:27.620 --> 06:29.815
Wait, Inuki!

06:38.865 --> 06:39.763
Hey, wait!

06:56.950 --> 06:59.043
Inuki, what's wrong?

07:10.830 --> 07:11.854
Beautiful...

07:12.966 --> 07:16.026
Inuki, how did you find
such a place?

07:16.135 --> 07:18.660
All right, I've decided
on this place!

07:27.680 --> 07:32.174
I was assigned a summer break
project to draw something.

07:32.285 --> 07:35.448
I got engrossed in
drawing that waterfall...

07:37.924 --> 07:40.518
Oh, this is a beautiful landscape.

07:40.627 --> 07:42.993
Nekoi, you went to
a wonderful place.

07:43.096 --> 07:45.360
Yeah!
I couldn't draw it well,

07:45.465 --> 07:47.797
but the real one
was even more pretty!

07:47.900 --> 07:50.198
Oh, it's drawn rather well.

07:50.303 --> 07:51.565
Where is this?

07:51.671 --> 07:54.265
Deep in the mountains
of Mitsumine.

07:54.374 --> 07:56.740
Mt. Mitsumine?

07:56.843 --> 07:59.539
Was there such a place
on Mt. Mitsumine?

07:59.646 --> 08:02.513
There's no waterfall
like that on Mt. Mitsumine.

08:02.615 --> 08:04.810
I've never heard of it, either.

08:04.917 --> 08:06.976
There is, too!
It's true!

08:07.086 --> 08:08.713
No, no, no way.

08:08.821 --> 08:10.584
I've been there
so many times!

08:10.690 --> 08:13.523
It's true.
I'm positive it's true!

08:13.626 --> 08:16.356
I'm sure Yuzuriha
imagined it and drew it.

08:16.462 --> 08:19.454
Yeah, here she goes
with her lies again.

08:19.565 --> 08:22.295
She always talks to that
invisible you-know-who.

08:22.402 --> 08:25.132
He's not invisible!
Inuki does exist!

08:25.238 --> 08:26.102
Right there!

08:28.207 --> 08:30.539
Here she goes
with the lies again.

08:30.643 --> 08:32.941
Keep lying and people'll
pull your tongue out!

08:33.046 --> 08:34.775
It's not a lie!
It's true!

08:34.881 --> 08:36.940
Stop! Don't you
feel sorry for her?

08:37.050 --> 08:37.982
Not at all.

08:38.084 --> 08:38.914
Stop it!

08:40.086 --> 08:41.917
All right, that's enough.

08:42.021 --> 08:44.319
In any case,
this is drawn very well.

08:44.424 --> 08:45.948
That should be enough.

08:48.995 --> 08:52.158
- Mitsuru, you drew a flower?
- Yes, it's a rose.

09:00.640 --> 09:02.574
Oh, welcome home...

09:07.046 --> 09:11.312
Grandma,
everyone calls me a liar.

09:12.418 --> 09:14.386
Inuki is right here, too!

09:15.488 --> 09:17.854
Everyone says I'm lying...

09:20.460 --> 09:22.758
Inuki really does exist.

09:22.862 --> 09:24.796
Right by your side.

09:24.897 --> 09:27.525
It's just that everyone
else can't see him.

09:27.633 --> 09:28.691
Why?

09:28.801 --> 09:30.496
Why can't they see him?

09:30.603 --> 09:33.436
Why am I the only one
who can see him?

09:33.539 --> 09:38.306
That's because Inuki is
a dog born just for you...

09:38.411 --> 09:41.778
...who will spend his
entire life at your side.

09:41.881 --> 09:44.509
Don't the other kids
have things like him?

09:44.617 --> 09:45.982
No, they don't.

09:46.085 --> 09:49.020
That is a power
that only you have.

09:49.122 --> 09:50.987
I don't want power like that!

09:51.090 --> 09:54.651
I want you to make Inuki so that
everyone else can see him, too!

09:54.761 --> 09:56.285
I can't do that.

09:57.897 --> 10:02.527
For with that power of yours,
you will become one of the stars...

10:02.635 --> 10:05.866
...who will determine
the fate of this world.

10:05.972 --> 10:10.341
I didn't understand much of
my grandma's story back then...

10:10.443 --> 10:15.312
But what I did understand was
I was somehow a special child.

10:21.521 --> 10:24.388
- To that waterfall?
- Yeah, let's all go together.

10:24.490 --> 10:27.516
It's not that far,
and I can bring a camera.

10:27.627 --> 10:31.893
If I show them pictures, I can
prove you're not lying, Yuzuriha.

10:31.998 --> 10:33.158
I wanna see, too.

10:33.266 --> 10:37.032
Nobody knows that there's
such a place on Mt. Mitsumine.

10:37.136 --> 10:38.194
Let's go.

10:38.304 --> 10:39.601
S-Sure.

10:39.705 --> 10:41.536
But will it be all right?

10:41.641 --> 10:42.573
Will what?

10:42.675 --> 10:44.700
It's really deep in the mountains.

10:44.811 --> 10:46.335
It's all right.

10:46.445 --> 10:49.175
You got there,
so I'm sure it'll be fine.

10:49.282 --> 10:50.909
Yeah, let's go!

10:51.017 --> 10:52.780
- Yeah...
- All right!

10:52.885 --> 10:54.216
Let's go Sunday!

10:54.320 --> 10:55.787
Go where?

11:07.767 --> 11:10.531
H-Hey, aren't we there yet?

11:10.636 --> 11:12.433
I'm dead tired already!

11:12.538 --> 11:13.800
It's just a bit more!

11:13.906 --> 11:15.203
It's further up!

11:15.308 --> 11:17.970
You've been saying it's
a bit more for a while!

11:19.478 --> 11:21.309
How far do we have to go?

11:21.414 --> 11:22.938
So it is a lie.

11:23.049 --> 11:25.745
They're waiting for us to give up.

11:25.852 --> 11:27.444
This pisses me off.

11:28.554 --> 11:30.886
Let's leave them alone
and keep going.

11:30.990 --> 11:33.686
Yeah, they decided to tag along.

11:33.793 --> 11:35.283
- Yup, yup!
- Let's go!

11:36.395 --> 11:37.589
Oh, hey!

11:37.697 --> 11:39.426
Wait!

11:39.532 --> 11:40.760
Hey, wait!

11:51.544 --> 11:54.012
Hey, where are you all going?

11:55.214 --> 11:58.115
Um, to a waterfall in this area.

11:59.552 --> 12:01.986
A waterfall?
You mean that thing?

12:05.224 --> 12:06.316
So small...

12:06.425 --> 12:09.724
No, there's one
that's much bigger!

12:09.829 --> 12:13.128
Oh, I've never seen such a thing.

12:13.232 --> 12:15.200
Will you kids be all right?

12:15.301 --> 12:16.632
It'll be dark soon!

12:17.703 --> 12:18.829
What should we do?

12:18.938 --> 12:22.305
If we're home too late,
Mom'll get mad at me...

12:22.408 --> 12:25.070
Yuzuriha, why don't
you just apologize?

12:25.177 --> 12:27.702
I know that this is all a lie.

12:27.813 --> 12:28.939
It's not a lie!

12:29.048 --> 12:30.606
I'm sick of hearing that!

12:30.716 --> 12:31.740
It's all right.

12:31.851 --> 12:33.819
It's scary when it's dark,
so let's go.

12:33.920 --> 12:36.980
Oh man,
this was a waste of time.

12:37.089 --> 12:38.078
Yeah, really.

12:38.190 --> 12:39.282
Let's go home.

12:42.194 --> 12:43.991
Ken, what are you doing?

12:47.566 --> 12:48.726
Is something wrong?

12:48.834 --> 12:50.495
I can hear something.

12:50.603 --> 12:52.537
From above here.

12:52.638 --> 12:54.230
See?

12:54.340 --> 12:56.103
What're you doing?
I'm goin'!

12:56.208 --> 12:57.766
Quiet!

12:57.877 --> 12:58.935
You're right.

12:59.045 --> 13:00.239
I hear something.

13:00.346 --> 13:01.711
See?

13:01.814 --> 13:02.746
I hear it...

13:03.849 --> 13:05.282
I hear it...

13:05.384 --> 13:07.079
From above here...

13:12.224 --> 13:13.623
A waterfall?

13:13.726 --> 13:14.590
Maybe...

13:14.694 --> 13:15.820
Guys...

13:15.928 --> 13:17.418
We're going on ahead!

13:17.530 --> 13:18.690
Wait!

13:24.370 --> 13:25.530
Let's go, Inuki!

13:36.082 --> 13:37.242
Be careful!

13:37.350 --> 13:39.682
It's dangerous to hurry so much!

13:39.785 --> 13:40.877
I hear it!

13:40.987 --> 13:42.284
It's from over here!

14:01.374 --> 14:02.568
Hiroshi!

14:02.675 --> 14:04.404
Help me!

14:04.510 --> 14:06.569
- Wait, I'll call for help!
- Help me!

14:08.681 --> 14:09.579
Hiroshi!

14:12.518 --> 14:13.917
Inuki!

14:14.020 --> 14:15.112
Save Hiroshi!

14:16.088 --> 14:17.419
Mommy!

14:17.523 --> 14:19.047
Help me!

14:19.158 --> 14:20.056
Help...

14:21.260 --> 14:22.557
Help me!

14:24.230 --> 14:25.128
Oh, no!

14:41.180 --> 14:42.408
What in the world?

14:44.116 --> 14:45.276
Hiroshi!

14:45.384 --> 14:46.681
Hiroshi!

14:46.786 --> 14:47.912
He's all right!

14:48.020 --> 14:49.044
Don't worry!

14:57.530 --> 14:59.464
Thanks, Inuki.

15:05.971 --> 15:08.235
I'm sorry my son troubled you.

15:08.340 --> 15:11.673
No, it was a good thing
that he wasn't badly hurt.

15:11.777 --> 15:15.474
To go that deep into
the mountains with no adults.

15:15.581 --> 15:18.607
I'm disgusted at how dumb he is.

15:18.717 --> 15:19.911
But...

15:20.019 --> 15:22.180
But Yuzuriha was
the one who asked.

15:25.858 --> 15:26.984
That's not true!

15:27.093 --> 15:29.152
I asked everyone to come!

15:29.261 --> 15:31.286
It's not Yuzuriha's fault!

15:31.397 --> 15:33.524
That's right. I asked, too.

15:33.632 --> 15:35.691
It's not Yuzuriha's fault!

15:35.801 --> 15:40.534
W-Well, in any case, we should
just be happy everyone was fine.

15:40.639 --> 15:43.733
- Yes, that's true.
- Yes, of course, of course.

15:43.843 --> 15:45.606
I'm sorry, Yuzuriha.

15:45.711 --> 15:47.269
Don't be so down.

15:49.181 --> 15:50.580
You heard it, right?

15:51.684 --> 15:53.743
The waterfall...

15:56.155 --> 15:57.884
Um...

15:57.990 --> 15:58.888
Well...

16:00.159 --> 16:02.593
I think I heard it, but...

16:08.200 --> 16:09.098
I see.

16:12.238 --> 16:15.969
In the end, nobody was
able to see that waterfall.

16:17.810 --> 16:20.040
Just like nobody could see Inuki.

16:21.714 --> 16:22.612
Nobody.

16:25.417 --> 16:29.217
Since then, nobody talked
about that waterfall...

16:29.321 --> 16:31.551
...and I stopped
talking about Inuki.

16:32.658 --> 16:36.560
If I didn't, my friends
would see me as strange...

16:36.662 --> 16:39.631
Inuki is a dog
that only I can see.

16:39.732 --> 16:41.859
It's lonely,
but that's how it is.

16:41.967 --> 16:44.333
But I really
did want everyone

16:44.436 --> 16:47.428
to know what a wonderful
dog Inuki is.

16:48.507 --> 16:50.031
That's true...

16:51.143 --> 16:55.443
That's why when I
saw you petting Inuki...

16:55.548 --> 16:57.675
I see.
You couldn't help it.

16:58.784 --> 17:00.877
But you know, little lady...

17:00.986 --> 17:05.286
I think it would've been enough
for him if you believed in him.

17:06.392 --> 17:10.488
He exists here because you believe
in him from your heart.

17:11.597 --> 17:12.962
That's what I think.

17:14.033 --> 17:16.297
Inuki should be
that sort of dog.

17:18.003 --> 17:19.493
Believe in him...

17:19.605 --> 17:20.867
...from my heart.

17:20.973 --> 17:22.099
That's right.

17:22.208 --> 17:25.268
If you believe,
Inuki will respond to that...

17:25.377 --> 17:27.311
...and never leave your side.

17:29.215 --> 17:32.548
I'll believe in him forever.

17:32.651 --> 17:33.640
Yeah.

17:33.752 --> 17:34.980
I'll believe, too.

17:36.922 --> 17:40.187
People who have powers
ordinary people don't have...

17:40.292 --> 17:42.852
...also feel pain
that they don't feel.

17:42.962 --> 17:44.020
But...

17:44.129 --> 17:48.156
...there should also be happiness
because you have that power.

17:48.267 --> 17:51.634
Being with Inuki wasn't
all bitter memories, right?

17:51.737 --> 17:53.466
Yes...

17:53.572 --> 17:54.504
Of course.

17:59.078 --> 18:02.206
Won't the person you were
waiting for be here soon?

18:02.314 --> 18:03.906
Oh, that's right!

18:04.016 --> 18:06.541
T-Thank you very much.

18:06.652 --> 18:10.850
Um, Kusanagi,
will you see me again?

18:10.956 --> 18:12.355
Sure.

18:12.458 --> 18:13.425
I don't mind.

18:13.525 --> 18:17.825
Then next time, I'd like to
hear lots of things about you!

18:17.930 --> 18:18.862
All right?

18:18.964 --> 18:20.955
Well, there's not much to tell...

18:21.066 --> 18:23.261
I'll look forward to it.

18:23.369 --> 18:24.927
So take care!

18:25.037 --> 18:25.935
Yeah!

18:30.075 --> 18:32.805
You take care too, little lady.

18:35.781 --> 18:40.241
Inuki, Mr. Kusanagi Shiyu
is such a wonderful person.

18:40.352 --> 18:43.480
I think I'm falling
in love with him.

18:44.757 --> 18:45.689
Um...

18:45.791 --> 18:47.986
Are you Yuzuriha Nekoi?

18:49.762 --> 18:51.423
Seiichiro!

18:54.867 --> 18:57.563
I'm Aoki.
Nice to meet you.

18:57.670 --> 19:00.366
I'm sorry that I was so late.

19:00.472 --> 19:02.201
No, it's all right.

19:02.308 --> 19:04.208
Are you done with your work?

19:04.310 --> 19:06.005
Yes, somehow.

19:06.111 --> 19:07.510
That's good.

19:07.613 --> 19:08.773
Thank you.

19:08.881 --> 19:12.180
I'd like to treat you to something
to make up for the wait.

19:12.284 --> 19:15.185
T-Then ice cream.

19:15.287 --> 19:16.185
Oh, no...

19:16.288 --> 19:18.017
I'm sorry, Mr. Saiki.

19:18.123 --> 19:19.886
No, it's all right.

19:19.992 --> 19:22.654
Let's have Seiichiro treat us.

19:22.761 --> 19:26.219
Sure, ice cream it is.

19:27.800 --> 19:32.066
But in any case, Daisuke,
you've grown so much.

19:32.171 --> 19:33.570
I'm rather impressed.

19:34.673 --> 19:38.939
I've known you since you carried
that little bag to kindergarten.

19:39.044 --> 19:40.511
He must've been cute!

19:40.612 --> 19:42.671
S-Seiichiro!

19:42.781 --> 19:44.248
It's all right.

19:44.350 --> 19:47.444
You're my one and only nephew.

19:47.553 --> 19:50.283
That's not what we're
here to talk about today.

19:50.389 --> 19:51.481
I know that.

19:52.925 --> 19:55.917
Yuzuriha, is your
grandmother doing well?

19:57.029 --> 19:59.156
You know my grandma?

19:59.264 --> 20:01.664
Yes, I've met her just once.

20:01.767 --> 20:04.167
Oh, I see...

20:04.269 --> 20:08.171
I'm sure she's lonely
after sending you off to Tokyo.

20:08.273 --> 20:09.171
Yes...

20:11.377 --> 20:15.939
But it's our destiny to protect
the Barrier Fields in Tokyo...

20:17.116 --> 20:21.485
And that time is definitely
creeping ever closer.

20:21.587 --> 20:22.952
Seiichiro...

20:24.123 --> 20:25.522
I knew it all along.

20:29.261 --> 20:33.698
I don't want this wonderful
world to be destroyed.

20:40.172 --> 20:41.730
Inuki.

20:41.840 --> 20:43.740
Today's such a wonderful day.

20:45.144 --> 20:48.409
We were able to meet
so many wonderful people.
